### Multi-Tenant SD-JWT Authentication API Examples
### Use with REST Client or similar HTTP client extensions

@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001
@contentType = application/json

###############################################################################
# 1. List All Tenants
###############################################################################

### Get all configured tenants
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/tenants
Accept: {{contentType}}

###############################################################################
# 2. Issue Tokens for Different Tenants
###############################################################################

### Issue token for ACME Corporation (2-hour lifetime)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "acme-corp",
  "subject": "user-12345",
  "claims": {
    "email": "alice@acme.com",
    "name": "Alice Smith",
    "role": "admin",
    "department": "engineering",
    "clearance": "top-secret"
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["email", "department", "clearance"],
  "tokenLifetimeSeconds": 3600
}

### Issue token for Contoso (1-hour lifetime)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "contoso",
  "subject": "employee-456",
  "claims": {
    "email": "bob@contoso.com",
    "role": "developer",
    "team": "platform"
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["email", "team"]
}

### Issue token for Fabrikam (30-minute lifetime)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "fabrikam",
  "subject": "contractor-789",
  "claims": {
    "email": "charlie@fabrikam.com",
    "role": "consultant",
    "project": "modernization"
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["email", "project"]
}

### Issue token for Woodgrove Bank (15-minute lifetime, financial tenant)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "woodgrove",
  "subject": "customer-42",
  "claims": {
    "email": "dave@example.com",
    "account_type": "premium",
    "account_number": "123456789",
    "balance": 50000.00
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["account_number", "balance"],
  "tokenLifetimeSeconds": 900
}

###############################################################################
# 3. Verify Tokens
###############################################################################

### Verify token (replace with actual SD-JWT from issue response)
### NOTE: Replace the presentation value with actual token from issue endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "presentation": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6ImFjbWUtMjAyNC0xMSJ9.eyJfc2QiOlsiU3lzdGVtLlN0cmluZ1tdIl0sInN1YiI6InVzZXItMTIzNDUiLCJpc3MiOiJodHRwczovL2V4YW1wbGUuY29tL3RlbmFudHMvYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwidGVuYW50X2lkIjoiYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzMxNTQ5NjAwLCJleHAiOjE3MzE1NTMyMDAsIm9yZyI6ImFjbWUtY29ycCIsIm9yZ19uYW1lIjoiQUNNRSBDb3Jwb3JhdGlvbiJ9.signature~disclosure~",
  "tenantId": "acme-corp"
}

### Verify token without tenant hint (auto-detect from token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "presentation": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6ImFjbWUtMjAyNC0xMSJ9.eyJfc2QiOlsiU3lzdGVtLlN0cmluZ1tdIl0sInN1YiI6InVzZXItMTIzNDUiLCJpc3MiOiJodHRwczovL2V4YW1wbGUuY29tL3RlbmFudHMvYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwidGVuYW50X2lkIjoiYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzMxNTQ5NjAwLCJleHAiOjE3MzE1NTMyMDAsIm9yZyI6ImFjbWUtY29ycCIsIm9yZ19uYW1lIjoiQUNNRSBDb3Jwb3JhdGlvbiJ9.signature~disclosure~"
}

###############################################################################
# 4. Error Cases
###############################################################################

### Try to issue token for invalid tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "nonexistent-tenant",
  "subject": "user-999",
  "claims": {
    "email": "test@example.com"
  }
}

### Try to issue token for disabled tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "test-disabled",
  "subject": "user-999",
  "claims": {
    "email": "test@example.com"
  }
}

### Try to verify invalid presentation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "presentation": "invalid.jwt.format~",
  "tenantId": "acme-corp"
}

### Try to verify with wrong tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "presentation": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6ImFjbWUtMjAyNC0xMSJ9.eyJfc2QiOlsiU3lzdGVtLlN0cmluZ1tdIl0sInN1YiI6InVzZXItMTIzNDUiLCJpc3MiOiJodHRwczovL2V4YW1wbGUuY29tL3RlbmFudHMvYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwidGVuYW50X2lkIjoiYWNtZS1jb3JwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzMxNTQ5NjAwLCJleHAiOjE3MzE1NTMyMDAsIm9yZyI6ImFjbWUtY29ycCIsIm9yZ19uYW1lIjoiQUNNRSBDb3Jwb3JhdGlvbiJ9.signature~disclosure~",
  "tenantId": "contoso"
}

###############################################################################
# 5. Key Rotation Scenarios
###############################################################################

### Issue token with current key (will use CurrentKeyId from config)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "contoso",
  "subject": "test-rotation",
  "claims": {
    "email": "rotation-test@contoso.com",
    "purpose": "key-rotation-demo"
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["email"]
}

### NOTE: After key rotation (adding contoso-key-v3 and updating CurrentKeyId):
### - New tokens will be issued with contoso-key-v3
### - Old tokens with contoso-key-v1 or contoso-key-v2 still verify (if keys remain in config)
### - Removing old keys from config will invalidate all tokens issued with those keys

###############################################################################
# 6. Selective Disclosure Examples
###############################################################################

### Issue token with multiple selective claims
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "acme-corp",
  "subject": "user-selective",
  "claims": {
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@acme.com",
    "phone": "+1-555-0123",
    "ssn": "123-45-6789",
    "address": {
      "street": "123 Main St",
      "city": "Boston",
      "state": "MA",
      "zip": "02101"
    }
  },
  "selectivelyDisclosableClaims": ["email", "phone", "ssn", "address.street", "address.zip"]
}

### NOTE: Holder can then create presentations revealing only specific claims
### For example:
### - Share email and phone for contact verification
### - Share address.city and address.state for location verification
### - Keep SSN completely hidden

###############################################################################
# 7. Tenant-Specific Features
###############################################################################

### ACME Corp: Long-lived token with default org claims
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "acme-corp",
  "subject": "long-lived-session",
  "claims": {
    "session_id": "sess-abc123",
    "ip": "203.0.113.42"
  }
}
### Result: Token automatically includes org="acme-corp", org_name="ACME Corporation"
### Max lifetime: 7200 seconds (2 hours)

### Woodgrove Bank: Short-lived token with compliance claims
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tokens/issue
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "tenantId": "woodgrove",
  "subject": "transaction-xyz",
  "claims": {
    "transaction_id": "txn-789",
    "amount": 1000.00
  }
}
### Result: Token automatically includes org_type="financial", compliance="regulated"
### Max lifetime: 900 seconds (15 minutes)

###############################################################################
# Notes:
#
# - All timestamps are Unix epoch seconds
# - SD-JWT format: jwt~disclosure~disclosure~...~keybinding (keybinding optional)
# - Tenant ID is automatically included in every token
# - Default claims from tenant config are merged automatically
# - Token lifetime cannot exceed tenant's MaxTokenLifetimeSeconds
###############################################################################
